.TH GARNER.YAML 5 "" "garner" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
garner.yaml \- garner configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/garner/garner.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR garner (1)
reads one YAML file.
It holds the decisions you make: what to serve, where to sync from and
how to sign.
Everything garner learns while running (packages, tokens, owners,
snapshots) lives in the database instead.
.PP
The default path is
.IR /etc/garner/garner.yaml ;
.B \-\-config
overrides it.
.B garner config validate
.RI [ FILE ]
checks a file.
It works offline and never opens the files that
.B *_file
keys point to, so it can run in CI.
.PP
.B SIGHUP
or
.B garner reload
reloads a running server.
An invalid file is rejected and logged, and the last good configuration
stays active.
See
.B CHANGES THAT NEED A RESTART
for the exceptions.
.PP
Unknown keys are errors, so a misspelled key fails validation instead of
being ignored.
The file must hold exactly one YAML document.
Validation reports every problem at once, each prefixed with its key path,
for example
.BR "sources[2].assets[0].suite: unknown suite \(dqnoble\(dq" .
.PP
Secrets are never written inline.
Point to them with a
.B *_file
or a
.B *_env
key.
.PP
Every key is optional unless marked
.BR required .
A key you leave out keeps its default.
The format sections,
.BR deb ,
.B rpm
and
.BR oci ,
are the exception: a format is enabled by its section being present, and
at least one is required.
An empty section
.RB ( deb:
or
.BR "deb: {}" )
enables the format with the defaults below.
.SH VALUE FORMATS
.TP
.I duration
A number with a unit:
.BR s ,
.BR m ,
.BR h .
There is no unit for days.
Examples:
.BR 30m ,
.BR 1h30m ,
.BR 168h .
.TP
.I size
Bytes, or a number with a unit:
.BR KB ", " MB ", " GB ", " TB
(powers of 1000) or
.BR KiB ", " MiB ", " GiB ", " TiB
(powers of 1024).
Examples:
.BR 2GiB ,
.BR 500MB ,
.BR 1048576 .
.TP
.I glob
.B *
matches any run of characters,
.B ?
one character,
.B [...]
a character class
.RB ( [^...]
negates it), and
.B \e
escapes the next character.
Examples:
.BR tool\-* ,
.BR *_amd64.deb .
.TP
.I listen address
.IB host : port
or
.BI : port\fR.
Examples:
.BR :8080 ,
.BR 127.0.0.1:9090 .
.SH SERVER
.TP
.BR listen " (\fIlisten address\fR, default " :8080 )
Where the HTTP server listens.
Changing it needs a restart.
.TP
.BR public_url " (\fIURL\fR, " required )
The URL clients use.
It goes into the apt and dnf client files and the UI, and its
host is the registry host that image names start with.
Must be an absolute
.B http
or
.B https
URL without a query or fragment.
A path is allowed, for example
.BR \%https://example.com/garner/ .
.TP
.BR client_name " (\fIname\fR, default " garner )
Prefix of the files clients install:
.IB name .sources\fR,
.IB name .repo\fR,
.I /usr/share/keyrings/\fIname\fP.gpg\fR,
and the dnf repo ID.
Lowercase letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.B _
and
.BR \- ;
must start with a letter or digit.
.TP
.BR trusted_proxies " (\fIlist of IPs or CIDR prefixes\fR, default " [] )
Reverse proxies whose
.B X\-Forwarded\-*
headers are honoured.
Authenticated requests are accepted only from loopback, or from one of
these with
.BR "X\-Forwarded\-Proto: https" .
Others get 403.
.TP
.BR allow_insecure_auth " (\fIbool\fR, default " false )
Accept authenticated requests over plain HTTP from any address.
Tokens then travel unencrypted, so use this only on an isolated lab
network.
.SH METRICS
.TP
.BR listen " (\fIlisten address\fR, default empty)"
Serve
.B /metrics
on a separate address.
When empty,
.B /metrics
is served on
.BR server.listen .
Changing it needs a restart.
.SH LOG
.TP
.BR format " (" json " or " text ", default " json )
Log line format.
.TP
.BR level " (" debug ", " info ", " warn " or " error ", default " info )
Lowest level that is logged.
.SH DATABASE
.TP
.BR url " (\fIURL\fR, default " \%sqlite:///var/lib/garner/garner.db )
The database.
Only SQLite is supported:
.B sqlite://
followed by an absolute path, so three slashes in total.
Keep the file on local disk, never on NFS.
Changing it needs a restart.
.SH STORAGE
.TP
.BR path " (\fIabsolute path\fR, default " /var/lib/garner )
Root of package blobs, snapshots and
.IR public/ ,
the directory clients are served from.
Changing it needs a restart.
.TP
.BR gc_grace " (\fIduration\fR, default " 10m )
How long a replaced snapshot is kept before deletion, so requests already
resolved through it can finish.
Must not be negative.
.TP
.BR index_history " (\fIduration\fR, default " 1h )
Index files of every snapshot published within this window are carried
into each new snapshot, so a client that fetched the signed top-level file
just before a publish can still fetch the indexes it lists.
The previous snapshot's index files are always carried over.
Must not be negative.
.TP
.BR snapshot_retention " (\fIinteger\fR, default " 30 )
How many snapshots are kept, newest first.
The current snapshot is always kept.
Must be at least 2.
.TP
.BR max_package_size " (\fIsize\fR, default " 2GiB )
Largest package garner accepts, from an upload or as a synced release
asset.
A larger upload gets 413; a larger asset is skipped and recorded as a
conflict.
Must be greater than zero.
.SH SIGNING
.TP
.BR keys " (\fIlist of keys\fR, default " [] )
OpenPGP keys.
All of them are published in
.B /key.asc
and
.BR /key.gpg ;
the first one signs.
When the list is empty,
.B garner init
generates an RSA 4096 key at
.I <storage.path>/signing/key.asc
and garner uses it.
.PP
Each entry of
.BR keys :
.TP
.BR key_file " (\fIpath\fR, " required )
Armored private key.
.TP
.BR passphrase_file " (\fIpath\fR, default empty)"
File holding the key's passphrase.
Leave it empty for a key without a passphrase, which is the default for
unattended signing.
.PP
To rotate keys: add the new key second, wait for clients to fetch the
keyring, move the new key first, then remove the old key.
Promoting a new key re\-signs every rpm package from its original.
.SH DEB
Present: garner serves an apt repository.
Absent: deb is disabled.
.TP
.BR architectures " (\fIlist\fR, default " [amd64] )
Debian architectures to publish.
Lowercase letters, digits and
.BR \- .
Don't list
.BR all :
architecture\-independent packages are published under every listed
architecture automatically.
.TP
.BR suites " (\fIlist\fR, default " [stable] )
Suites to publish.
Letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.B _
and
.BR \- .
The first suite, or
.B stable
if listed, is the default: uploads without
.B \-\-suite
and sources without asset rules use it, and its client file is served at
the root, the others below
.IR clients/<suite>/ .
.SH RPM
Present: garner serves dnf repositories.
Absent: rpm is disabled.
.PP
rpm also needs
.BR createrepo_c ,
.BR rpmsign ,
.B gpg
and
.B gpgconf
on
.BR PATH .
With the section present and a tool missing,
.B serve
refuses to start and names the missing tools.
.PP
Removing a format's section keeps its packages stored, but no longer serves
them, and
.B serve
logs a warning about them at every start; adding the section back serves
them again, re-signed if the key changed meanwhile.
Uploads and synced assets of a disabled format are rejected.
.TP
.BR architectures " (\fIlist\fR, default " [x86_64] )
rpm architectures to publish.
Lowercase letters, digits and
.BR _ .
Don't list
.BR noarch ;
it is implicit, as
.B all
is for deb.
.B i686
is multilib: its packages are listed in the
.B x86_64
repository, where dnf on x86_64 hosts finds them, so it requires
.B x86_64
and gets no repository of its own.
.TP
.BR releases " (\fIlist\fR, default " [stable] )
Releases to publish.
Same rules and default handling as
.BR deb.suites .
.SH OCI
Present: garner is a container registry at
.I /v2/
on the host root, which
.BR "docker push" ,
.B docker pull
and other OCI clients use.
Absent: images are disabled.
Images are pushed or synced from registries, never uploaded with
.BR "garner upload" .
Pushes need a token with the
.B upload
scope, used with
.BI "docker login " host " \-u " "token name"
and the token's secret as the password.
.TP
.BR retention " (\fIinteger\fR, default " 10 )
Untagged manifests kept per image name, newest first, besides every
tagged one.
A manifest becomes untagged when its tag moves to a newer push;
deployments that pin digests keep working until it ages out.
.B 0
keeps all.
Also applies to images from a registry source that does not set its own
.BR retention ;
.B defaults.retention
does not apply to images.
.TP
.BR upload_expiry " (\fIduration\fR, default " 24h )
How long a pushed blob that no manifest uses yet, and an idle upload
session, are kept before GC removes them.
Must be at least
.BR 1m .
.SH DEFAULTS
Settings for every source that does not override them.
.B retention
also applies to uploaded packages.
.TP
.BR retention " (\fIinteger\fR, default " 3 )
Versions kept per package name, distribution and architecture.
Older versions leave future snapshots; pinned packages are always kept.
Must be at least 1.
.TP
.BR poll_interval " (\fIduration\fR, default " 1h )
How often a source is polled, with \(+-10% jitter.
Must be at least
.BR 1m .
.TP
.BR verify " (" opportunistic " or " required ", default " opportunistic )
Checksum policy.
An asset is checked against the forge's digest or the release's checksum
file when one exists, and a mismatch always rejects it.
.B opportunistic
accepts assets without a checksum and marks them unverified.
.B required
rejects them.
.TP
.BR approval " (" auto " or " manual ", default " auto )
With
.BR manual ,
new packages are stored as held and published only after
.BR "garner approve" .
.TP
.BR prereleases " (\fIbool\fR, default " false )
Sync pre\-releases too.
Drafts are never synced.
.TP
.BR min_release_age " (\fIduration\fR, default " 0s )
How old a synced release must be before garner processes it, so a
compromised release has time to be noticed and pulled first.
The age runs from the release's publish time or, on GitHub and Forgejo,
from the upload of its newest package asset if that is later.
On GitLab it runs from the later of the release's creation and its
.BR released_at .
.B 0s
turns the wait off.
Must not be negative.
A younger release is deferred: later polls check it again, and
.B garner status
lists it.
A source's first run takes the latest release that is old enough; newer
releases follow as each one ages, so a new source can publish several
recent versions over its first days.
Assets attached after publishing are waited for, then wait for their own
age; on GitLab, whose links carry no time, an old-enough release is
processed as it is and links added later are not picked up.
A release without a publish time waits until
.B garner sync \-\-ignore\-age
lets it through.
Uploads are not affected.
.SH FORGES
A list of forges that sources sync from.
There are none by default.
.TP
.BR name " (\fIname\fR, " required )
Name that sources refer to.
Lowercase letters, digits,
.B _
and
.BR \- ;
must start with a letter or digit; unique.
.TP
.BR type " (" required )
.BR github ,
.BR forgejo ,
.B gitea
(an alias of
.BR forgejo )
or
.BR gitlab .
.TP
.BR url " (\fIhttps URL\fR, default empty)"
The forge's base URL.
Required except for
.BR github ,
where empty means github.com; set it to use GitHub Enterprise Server.
Must be
.BR https ,
because tokens are sent to it.
.TP
.BR token_env " (\fIvariable name\fR, default empty)"
Environment variable holding the API token.
.TP
.BR token_file " (\fIpath\fR, default empty)"
File holding the API token; surrounding whitespace is trimmed.
Set
.B token_env
or
.BR token_file ,
not both.
With neither, requests are unauthenticated.
.TP
.BR ca_file " (\fIpath\fR, default empty)"
PEM file with the CA certificates that sign the forge's TLS certificate.
TLS verification can't be turned off.
.TP
.BR max_concurrent " (\fIinteger\fR, default " 4 )
Most requests in flight to this forge at once.
Must be at least 1.
.TP
.BR proxy " (\fIURL\fR, default empty)"
Proxy for this forge's requests: an
.BR http ,
.B https
or
.B socks5
URL.
When empty,
.B HTTPS_PROXY
and
.B NO_PROXY
from the environment apply.
.PP
The token is sent only to the forge's own scheme, host and port.
Asset links that point elsewhere are fetched without it.
For a private repository, set
.B url
to the address the forge puts in its asset links
(Forgejo's ROOT_URL, GitLab's external_url);
otherwise the downloads fail without the token and are retried on every poll.
.SH REGISTRIES
A list of OCI registries that registry sources sync images from.
There are none by default.
.TP
.BR name " (\fIname\fR, " required )
Name that sources refer to.
Same rules as forge names.
.TP
.BR url " (\fIhttps URL\fR, " required )
The registry's address without a path, such as
.I https://ghcr.io
or, for Docker Hub,
.IR https://registry\-1.docker.io .
Must be
.BR https .
.TP
.BR username " (\fIstring\fR, default empty)"
User name sent with the token.
Needs
.B token_env
or
.BR token_file .
.TP
.BR token_env " (\fIvariable name\fR, default empty)"
Environment variable holding the password or token.
.TP
.BR token_file " (\fIpath\fR, default empty)"
File holding the password or token; surrounding whitespace is trimmed.
Set
.B token_env
or
.BR token_file ,
not both.
With neither, garner pulls anonymously.
.TP
.BR auth_hosts " (\fIlist of hosts\fR, default " [] )
Hosts besides the registry's own that may receive the credentials as
token endpoints:
.I auth.docker.io
for Docker Hub, the GitLab host for a GitLab registry.
ghcr.io needs none.
.TP
.BR ca_file ", " max_concurrent ", " proxy
As for forges.
.PP
Credentials go only to the registry's host and to a token endpoint on it
or in
.BR auth_hosts .
A registry that names another token endpoint gets an error, not the
credentials.
Blob downloads redirected to other hosts, as ghcr.io and Docker Hub do to
their CDNs, are fetched without credentials.
Docker Hub limits anonymous pulls per address, so give a Docker Hub
registry credentials.
.SH SOURCES
A list of places to sync from.
There are none by default.
A forge source is one repository
.RB ( repo ),
a GitHub or Forgejo organization
.RB ( org ),
or a GitLab group
.RB ( group );
set exactly one of the three.
A registry source is one image of a registry; see
.BR "REGISTRY SOURCES" .
.TP
.BR name " (\fIname\fR, " required )
Unique name, used in logs, metrics, status and
.BI "garner sync " name\fR.
Same rules as forge names.
.TP
.BR forge " (\fIforge name\fR, " required )
The
.B forges[].name
to sync from.
.TP
.BR repo " (\fIowner\fB/\fIname\fR, default empty)"
A single repository.
GitLab paths may have more parts
.RI ( group/sub/project ).
.TP
.BR org " (\fIname\fR, default empty)"
A GitHub or Forgejo organization; every repository in it is synced.
New repositories are picked up on the next poll.
.TP
.BR group " (\fIpath\fR, default empty)"
A GitLab group, synced like
.BR org .
.TP
.BR owns " (\fIlist of globs\fR, default " [] )
Package names this source reserves.
Only this source may deliver them, also against uploads.
Globs of two sources must not be able to match the same name; validation
names an example if they do.
.TP
.BR assets " (\fIlist of rules\fR, default " [] )
Which deb suite or rpm release each asset goes to; see
.BR "ASSET RULES" .
.TP
.BR include " (\fIlist of globs\fR, default " [] )
For
.B org
and
.B group
sources only: sync only repositories whose name (without the owner)
matches one of these.
Empty means all.
.TP
.BR exclude " (\fIlist of globs\fR, default " [] )
Skip repositories whose name matches, and skip assets whose file name
matches.
Matching assets are never downloaded.
.TP
.BR checksums " (\fIlist of globs\fR, default " [] )
File names of a release's checksum files.
They replace the built\-in names
.RB ( checksums.txt ,
.BR *_checksums.txt ,
.BR SHA256SUMS ,
.BR *.sha256 ).
.TP
.BR archived " (\fIbool\fR, default " false )
Also sync archived repositories of an
.B org
or
.BR group .
.TP
.BR forks " (\fIbool\fR, default " false )
Also sync forks in an
.B org
or
.BR group .
.TP
.BR recursive " (\fIbool\fR, default " true )
Walk GitLab subgroups.
Only valid on GitLab
.B group
sources.
.PP
A source can also set
.BR retention ,
.BR poll_interval ,
.BR verify ,
.BR approval ,
.B prereleases
and
.BR min_release_age ,
which override
.B defaults
for that source only.
The same rules apply.
.PP
Some asset names are always skipped:
.BR *.src.rpm ,
.B \%*\-dbgsym*
and
.BR \%*\-debuginfo* ,
and files without the extension of an enabled format
.RB ( .deb ,
.BR .rpm ).
.PP
On its first run, a source syncs only the latest release of each
repository.
Later runs pick up every release published since then.
.SS REGISTRY SOURCES
A registry source sets
.B registry
in place of
.BR forge .
.TP
.BR registry " (\fIregistry name\fR, " required )
The
.B registries[].name
to sync from.
.TP
.BR image " (\fIimage name\fR, " required )
The image's path on the registry, such as
.I avesst/tool
or, on Docker Hub,
.IR library/alpine .
.TP
.BR tags " (\fIlist of globs\fR, " required )
Tags to sync.
Every matching tag is synced on the first run, so keep them narrow.
.TP
.BR as " (\fIimage name\fR, default " image )
The name the image is served under.
.PP
.BR owns ,
.BR retention ,
.BR poll_interval ,
.B approval
and
.B min_release_age
work as for forge sources; the forge source keys are not allowed.
A registry source's
.B owns
reserves image names, and a forge source's reserves package names, so the
same glob in both is no conflict.
.PP
Each poll lists the image's tags and resolves the matching ones.
A digest garner has not stored is downloaded whole, every platform of an
index included, and every blob is checked against its digest.
A tag that moves upstream moves in garner too; the digest it pointed at
becomes untagged and is kept per
.BR retention .
A tag deleted upstream stays in garner.
A digest garner has processed is never synced again once it is removed,
whether by retention, a rollback or a delete, so a rollback holds until
the tag moves upstream to a new digest.
.PP
With
.BR min_release_age ,
the wait runs from when garner first saw the digest under the tag.
Each poll applies the newest digest seen under the tag that is old enough,
so a tag upstream moves more often than the minimum age still advances.
A digest upstream withdraws, by moving the tag back before it is old
enough, is never applied.
A tag moves only when upstream moves it: after a rollback, or after an
admin deletes the tag, it stays as it is until upstream points it at a new
digest.
Two registry sources may not serve images under the same name.
Changing a source's
.B as
syncs its images under the new name on the next poll.
.BI "garner sync " source " \-\-ignore\-age " tag
lets a waiting digest through.
With
.BR "approval: manual" ,
a new digest is held without its tag; after
.BR "garner approve" ,
the next poll points the tag at it.
.SS ASSET RULES
Each entry of
.BR assets :
.TP
.BR match " (\fIglob\fR, " required )
Asset file names this rule applies to.
.TP
.BR suite " (\fIsuite name\fR, default empty)"
Target for
.B .deb
assets.
Must be listed in
.BR deb.suites ,
so
.B deb
must be configured.
.TP
.BR release " (\fIrelease name\fR, default empty)"
Target for
.B .rpm
assets.
Must be listed in
.BR rpm.releases ,
so
.B rpm
must be configured.
.PP
Set
.BR suite ,
.B release
or both.
Rules are evaluated in order.
The first rule whose
.B match
fits the asset name and that sets a target for the asset's format wins, so
a
.B *
rule with only
.B suite
does not catch rpm assets.
.IP \(bu 2
With no rules at all, every asset goes to the default suite or release:
.B stable
if listed, else the first one.
.IP \(bu 2
With rules, an asset that no rule places is skipped and not downloaded.
.IP \(bu 2
If two assets of one release end up as the same package, version,
architecture and distribution, both are skipped and a conflict is
recorded.
.SH CHANGES THAT NEED A RESTART
A reload applies everything except these keys.
Changing them makes the reload fail with a message naming the keys, and
the running configuration stays active until you restart:
.BR server.listen ,
.BR metrics.listen ,
.BR database.url ,
.BR storage.path ,
and adding or removing a format section
.RB ( deb ,
.BR rpm ,
.BR oci ).
.PP
A reload restarts only the sources whose effective settings changed,
including inherited defaults and their forge's or registry's settings.
The others keep their schedule.
.SH EXAMPLE
A small setup: one internal Forgejo, one repository with separate Ubuntu
and EL9 builds, and a whole organization synced to
.BR stable .
.PP
.RS
.nf
server:
  public_url: https://packages.example.com
  trusted_proxies: ["10.0.0.5"]

storage:
  path: /var/lib/garner

deb:
  architectures: [amd64, arm64]
  suites: [stable, noble]

rpm:
  architectures: [x86_64]
  releases: [stable, el9]

forges:
  \- name: forgejo
    type: forgejo
    url: https://git.example.com
    token_file: /run/credentials/garner.service/forgejo\-token

sources:
  \- name: tool
    forge: forgejo
    repo: platform/tool
    owns: ["tool", "tool\-*"]
    assets:
      \- match: "*_ubuntu24.04*.deb"
        suite: noble
      \- match: "*.el9.*.rpm"
        release: el9
      \- match: "*"
        suite: stable
        release: stable

  \- name: platform
    forge: forgejo
    org: platform
    exclude: ["legacy\-*", "*\-musl*"]
    approval: manual
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR garner (1)
